Subject: [PATCH 08/37] docs: deep-idle research: awake timer sources,
 on-demand DCP design

The awake wakeups come from user space: one polling process arms about
80% of the hrtimers, and no kernel timer stands out. The other domains left
on in s2idle are parents of always-on domains. Write down why starting the
external DCPs on demand is not built yet, the hook points it needs, and the
experiments that should come first.

